course: dictionary
lesson: 14888
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so read the sentence to find the right one. «The little girl recognized her grandad at the station, even from far away.» Here recognized means knew who he was, because she had seen him before.
explain: «He recognized his mistake and said sorry.» Recognized here means accepted or admitted that something is true. The clue is mistake: you can admit a mistake, but you cannot see one with your eyes. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Recognized can also be a describing word, as in «a recognized qualification», which means one that is officially accepted. In Britain you may see it spelled recognised with an s. Both spellings are correct.
fact: Recognized is the past form of the verb recognize.
fact: «Recognized» can mean knew who someone was or what something was, because you had seen or heard it before.
fact: «Recognized» can mean accepted or admitted that something is true.
fact: «Recognized» can also mean officially accepted, or showed thanks for and praised someone's good work.
fact: In British English the word is often spelled recognised, with an s.
exercise: «The dog recognized the sound of its owner's car and ran to the gate.» What does recognized mean here? | *Knew it because it had heard it before | Admitted that the car was true | Officially approved the car | Praised the car for its speed
exercise: «She recognized that she had broken the vase and said sorry.» What does recognized mean here? | Had never seen it before | Gave a prize for her work | Lost it somewhere in the house | *Admitted that something was true
exercise: «The school recognized Amir for his hard work with a certificate.» What does recognized mean here? | Made a copy of his book | Stopped him from leaving | Forgot his name | *Showed thanks for and praised his work
test: In «a recognized qualification», what does recognized mean? | *Officially accepted | Praised for good work | Knew who it was | Forgotten
test: «Ella recognized her best friend's voice on the phone straight away.» What does recognized mean here? | Got a reward | Admitted a mistake | Officially accepted | *Knew who it was, because she had heard it before
exam: Which sentence uses recognized to mean accepted or admitted that something is true? | «The school recognized Leo for his kindness.» | «She recognized her friend across the playground.» | *«He recognized his mistake and apologized.» | «The old man recognized the song.»
